                                                                        <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionIRI> <https://posccaesar.org/ontology/quality-aspect/0.1.0/ont/core-owl>;
                                                                        <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionInfo> "0.1.0";
                                                                        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> """Defines property aspects of lis:Quality as OWL ontology
Background:
The Industrial Data Ontology (IDO) already establishes a clear distinction between properties (lis:Quality) and values (lis:QualityDatum).
Building on this foundation, this ontology introduces aspects to further refine the semantics of properties (lis:Quality).
Aspects enable a more granular and standardized representation of property-related information,
allowing for precise classification and contextualization of properties (lis:Quality) that describe the property itself,
independent of its specific values.

This ontology is inspired by and extends the plm ontology from POSC Caesar Association (PCA).""".
    <https://posccaesar.org/ontology/quality-datum-aspect/0.1.0/ont/core-owl> <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/rights> "Copyright POSC Caesar Association";
                                                                              <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-05-07";
                                                                              <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> <https://orcid.org/0009-0003-7263-9946>;
                                                                              <http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/>;
                                                                              <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2026-06-01";
                                                                              <http://purl.org/dc/terms/publisher> <https://www.posccaesar.org/>;
                                                                              <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "QualityDatum Value Aspect Extension Ontology OWL";
                                                                              <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/preferredNamespacePrefix> "lis-ext-qd-asp-owl";
                                                                              <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/preferredNamespaceUri> <https://posccaesar.org/ontology/quality-datum-aspect/0.1.0/rdl/>;
                                                                              a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology>;
                                                                              rdfs:label "QualityDatum Value Aspect Extension Ontology OWL";
                                                                              rdfs:seeAlso <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/plm/ont/core>;
                                                                              <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#imports> <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/ont/core>,
                                                                                                                      <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/>;
                                                                              <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionIRI> <https://posccaesar.org/ontology/quality-datum-aspect/0.1.0/ont/core-owl>;
                                                                              <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionInfo> "0.1.0";
                                                                              <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> """Defines value aspects of lis:QualityDatum as OWL ontology
Background:
The Industrial Data Ontology (IDO) already establishes a clear distinction between properties (lis:Quality) and values (lis:QualityDatum).
Building on this foundation, this ontology introduces aspects to further refine the semantics of values (lis:QualityDatum).
Aspects enable a more granular and standardized representation of value-related information,
allowing for precise classification and contextualization of characteristics that describe specific values (lis:QualityDatum),
such as ranges, thresholds, or other value-specific attributes.

This ontology aligns with IEC 61360-1, particularly its LEVEL_TYPE concept (MIN, NOM, TYP, MAX),
which is now implemented more flexibly by representing each role as a separate class and
supporting all four values to enable precise semantic composition of value aspects.

This ontology is inspired by and extends the plm ontology from POSC Caesar Association (PCA).""".
    <https://posccaesar.org/ontology/quality-datum-data-type/0.1.0/ont/core-owl> <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/rights> "Copyright POSC Caesar Association";
                                                                                 <http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> <https://orcid.org/0009-0003-7263-9946>;
                                                                                 <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2021-02-15";
                                                                                 <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> <https://orcid.org/0009-0005-9639-4327>;
                                                                                 <http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/>;
                                                                                 <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2026-06-01";
                                                                                 <http://purl.org/dc/terms/publisher> <https://www.posccaesar.org/>;
                                                                                 <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "QualityDatum Data Type Extension Ontology OWL";
                                                                                 <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/preferredNamespacePrefix> "lis-ext-qd-dt-owl";
                                                                                 <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/preferredNamespaceUri> <https://posccaesar.org/ontology/quality-datum-data-type/0.1.0/rdl/>;
                                                                                 a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology>;
                                                                                 rdfs:label "QualityDatum Data Type Extension Ontology OWL";
                                                                                 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#imports> <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/ont/core>,
                                                                                                                         <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/>;
                                                                                 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionIRI> <https://posccaesar.org/ontology/quality-datum-data-type/0.1.0/ont/core-owl>;
                                                                                 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionInfo> "0.1.0";
                                                                                 <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> """Defines basic data types of lis:QualityDatum in accordance with IEC61360-1 as OWL ontology
Background:
The Industrial Data Ontology (IDO) already establishes a clear distinction between properties (lis:Quality) and values (lis:QualityDatum).
This ontology extends the data type modeling for lis:QualityDatum by defining specific data types in accordance with IEC 61360-1.
The class names and labels are oriented towards the corresponding XSD data types to ensure consistency with standard data representations and interoperability.
This ontology aligns with the data type definitions in IEC 61360-1. """.
